name:Adoro te devote;
office-part:Hymnus;
mode:5;
book:The Liber Usualis, 1961, p. 1855 & Chants of the Church, 1956, p. 81 & Liber antiphonarius, 1960, p. 100*;
transcriber:Andrew Hinkley;
%%
(cb3) O[O memorial of the death of the Lord](d') me(f)mo(h')ri(h)á(hi)le(h.) (,) mor(g')tis(f) Dó(e')mi(d)ni,(d.) (;)
Pa(d')nis[living bread supplying life to men](f) vi(h')vus(h) vi(hi)tam(h.) (,) prae(g')stans(f) hó(e')mi(d)ni,(d.) (:)
Prae[supply to my mind](h)sta(h) me(ij)ae(k) men(kj)ti[of thee to live](h.) (,) de(i') te(h) ví(g')ve(f)re,(e.) (;)
Et[and thee that always sweet to taste](f') te(h) il(g')li(f) sem(e[ll:1]d)per(e.) (,) dul(f')ce(d) sá(e')pe(d)re.(d.) (::) 

6. Pi[ ~ O loving pelican, O Jesus Lord](d')e(f) pel(h')li(h)cá(hi)ne,(h.) (,) Je(g')su(f) Dó(e')mi(d)ne,(d.) (;)
Me[filthy me](d') im(f)mún(h')dum(h) mun[do thou cleanse by thy blood](hi)da(h.) (,) tu(g')o(f) sán(e')gui(d)ne,(d.) (:)
Cu(h)jus[of which one drop safe to make](h) u(ij)na(k) stil(kj)la(h.) (,) sal(i')vum(h) fá(g')ce(f)re(e.) (;)
To[all the world ~ can ~ from every evil deed](f')tum(h) mun(g')dum(f) quit(e[ll:1]d) ab(e) o(f')mni(d) scé(e')le(d)re.(d.) (::) 

